<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves fall to $1.377 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves fall to $1.377 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves fell to $1.377 billion as of January 23 from $1.474 billion a week earlier, compared to $2.384 billion on January 25, 1996, the State Bank of Pakistan said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Following is the weekly foreign exchange reserves position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		JAN 23     JAN 16     JAN 25, 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL			   1,377	1,474	2,384</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan	     492	  444	1,289</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan	197	  341	  374</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion	676	  676	  707</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights	 12	   13	   14</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
